---
description: No code comments of any kind; enforced by the brr/no-comments oxlint rule
alwaysApply: true
---

# No code comments

- Don't write comments in any code: line, block, JSDoc, JSX `{/* */}`, triple-slash, `@ts-expect-error`/`@ts-ignore`, `oxlint-disable`, `TODO`. The only exception is a shebang line.
- `brr/no-comments` (in `tools/oxlint-plugin`) reports every comment in JS and TS files, and `pnpm lint` fails CI. Don't turn it off, add overrides or exclude files to get around it.
- **Instead of a comment:**
  - Choose names, types, small functions, and named constants for magic values.
  - Use a test to pin a non-obvious constraint.
  - Use `types` in tsconfig in place of triple-slash references.
  - Fix type errors properly; never suppress them.
- Put rationale in the commit message, the PR description or `docs/`. Put task lists in the tracker.
- JSON, YAML and HTML config files carry no comments either, even where the format allows them.
